{"benchmark": "ifeval", "task_id": "1001", "sample_idx": 18, "model_name": "mistralai/mixtral-8x7b-instruct-v0.1", "content": " Upon the distant shore of Japan dost thou wish to set foot? Fear not, for I shall craft a journey fit for royalty.\n\n\nHark! On the morrow, depart from thy dwelling and seek the skies. A metal bird shall bear thee to the land of the rising sun. Land in Tokyo, the bustling metropolis, where modernity and tradition intertwine.\n\n\nOn the second day, visit the Meiji Shrine, dedicated to the spirits of Emperor Meiji and Empress Shoken. Pay thy respects and explore the lush forest that surrounds the sacred grounds. In the afternoon, wander through the bustling streets of Harajuku and Shibuya, where youth culture and fashion reign supreme.\n\n\nOn the third day, embark on a pilgrimage to Nikko, home of the Toshogu Shrine, mausoleum of Tokugawa Ieyasu, the founder of the Tokugawa shogunate. Marvel at the intricate carvings and the beauty of the surrounding nature.\n\n\nOn the fourth day, retreat to Hakone, a hot spring paradise. Relax and rejuvenate in the soothing waters, and enjoy a boat ride on Lake Ashi. If the weather permits, gaze upon the majesty of Mount Fuji.\n\n\nOn the fifth day, return to Tokyo and explore the historical district of Asakusa. Visit the Senso-ji temple, Tokyo's oldest temple, and indulge in some street food. In the evening, witness the dazzling spectacle of the Shinjuku Kabuki-cho district, where neon lights and lively entertainment abound.\n \\_\n\nFare thee well, brave traveler! May this itinerary bring thee joy and adventure in the land of Japan.", "logprobs": [{"token": "Upon", "logprob": -0.308956116437912}, {"token": "the", "logprob": -0.021099278703331947}, {"token": "distant", "logprob": -1.5090998411178589}, {"token": "shore", "logprob": -0.9966671466827393}, {"token": "of", "logprob": -8.583032467868179e-06}, {"token": "Japan", "logprob": -0.006945632863789797}, {"token": "d", "logprob": -1.2943722009658813},